    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_490fb3cf",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: let_me_be_clear_oh; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image shows former U.S. President Barack Obama smiling while holding a microphone, with the text 'let me be clear..' above and 'uh..' below. The juxtaposition implies a moment of awkwardness or hesitation, often used humorously to suggest someone is about to say something important but is struggling to articulate it. While not inherently abusive or hateful, the meme's intent is to mock or ridicule the person's perceived inability to deliver a clear message, which can be seen as harmful if it targets an individual's competence or communication skills. The meme does not contain any explicit toxic content related to protected characteristics, but its humor relies on the audience's perception of the subject's speech or demeanor, which may be interpreted as demeaning in certain contexts.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_0c6f1c26"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
